From: Jakob Haufe <sur5r@sur5r.net>
Subject: Use AX_COMPILER_FLAGS instead of GNOME_COMPILE_WARNINGS

GNOME_COMPILE_WARNINGS comes from gnome-common, which is deprecated and
not needed for anything else. ax_COMPILER_FLAGS from autoconf-archive
provides the same warning flags without gnome-common.

Taken from the Debian glabels package (0004-gnome-common-cleanup).

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@ AC_SEARCH_LIBS([strerror],[cposix])
 AC_PROG_CC
 AC_PROG_INSTALL
 
-GNOME_COMPILE_WARNINGS
+AX_COMPILER_FLAGS
 
 AC_PATH_PROG(GLIB_GENMARSHAL,         glib-genmarshal)
 AC_PATH_PROG(GDK_PIXBUF_CSOURCE,      gdk-pixbuf-csource)
